This is my first project back

Problem Statement: 
    I want a application to keep track of all my trading and investments
    at a glance

Libraries used:
    pandas (For working with labeled data efficiently)
    yfinance (For financial and market data from Yahoo Finance)
    streamlit (Turns python scripts into interactive webapps)
    numpy (For mathematical functions)
    scipy (For scientific and numerical computation tools)

db.py is to create the database in sqlite and store all the values needed that I want to track.

prices.py uses the yfinance library to read Yahoo Finance financial data. (Hopes to be changed to TradingView or other platforms data in the future.)

analytics.py for my functions to calculate/analyze the data I want to see. (Functions to be put in separate files in the future when more robust.)

app.py is the main app body in which everything runs through using streamlit. (Hoping to be changed to using C, HTML, CSS, etc. for more robust website and better UX/UI in the future.)

engine.py contains the portfolio's transactions and valuation calculations

Run: streamlit run app.py

25/11/2026: Transaction made into db, next step is to validate for ticker symbol as typing it incorrectly returns a ValueError. Homework: Learn pandas and yfinance libraries